# Allowlist: the docker build context is the repo root, and NOTHING else may
# ride along. Two reasons this matters:
#  - .sc/ holds DECRYPTED secrets after `sc secrets reveal` runs in CI — it
#    must never enter a build context (and with the `COPY . .` Go-builder
#    stages in github-actions.Dockerfile / cloud-helpers.aws.Dockerfile, it
#    would land in cacheable builder layers, not just the context tarball).
#  - the context used to ship docs/, dist/, .git/ etc. for a build that needs
#    none of them.
# `bin` stays allowed: github-actions-staging.Dockerfile COPYs ./bin/… (built
# on the host by welder in build-staging.yml).
*
!cmd
!pkg
!internal
!go.mod
!go.sum
!tools.go
!bin
